# Secrets / local state — never publish
# Both SHIP.md files name .env.* and secrets/ as guarded. Until 2026-08-11 only
# `.env` was, so a `.env.local` or `secrets/infoblox.json` was committable while
# the playbook said otherwise. The negation must follow the glob: .env.example is
# the tracked template and .env.* would otherwise swallow it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
.vault-passphrase
dns_clients_cache.json
ruvector.db
server.log
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
.venv.broken/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
.playwright-mcp/

# Claude Code / AI tooling (local only)
.claude/
.impeccable/
.mcp.json

# Internal AI training / planning docs (not for end users)
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
DESIGN.md
COLOR_CONTRACT.md
SKILLS.md
MCP.md
PRODUCT.md
DAILY_CHANGELOG.md
brainstorms/
plans/
.mockups/
docs/change-reporting.md
docs/CONTEXT.md
docs/design-workflow.md
docs/PLANNING.md
docs/TESTING.md

# Proof/screenshot artifacts
*-verify.png
*_proof.png

# Node / frontend build (new scaffold)
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# Playwright
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/

# Alert suppression state — runtime data, not a secret, never committed
backend/data/alert_state.json
backend/data/alert_state.json.tmp

# Audit log — runtime data (hash-chained, tamper-evident), never committed
backend/data/audit_log.jsonl

# Same runtime state, at the paths THIS app actually writes. server.py puts them
# in _STATE_DIR = dirname(VAULT_FILE): under Docker that's the /vault volume, but
# running server.py directly for local dev resolves it to the REPO ROOT — where
# the backend/data/ rules above don't match and `git add -A` would sweep them in.
# audit_log.jsonl carries actor identities and request paths; never commit it.
/audit_log.jsonl
/alert_state.json
/alert_state.json.tmp
/first_seen.json
/first_seen.json.tmp

# encrypted vault — never commit
vault.json
scripts/out_*.json
scripts/out_*.txt
scripts/catalog_*.py
# ...but the nightly MCP drift-check workflow diffs three baselines (tools,
# services, cubes), so it needs the three catalog scripts it runs and the
# three baseline snapshots it diffs against tracked.
!scripts/catalog_tools.py
!scripts/out_tools.json
!scripts/catalog_services.py
!scripts/out_services.json
!scripts/catalog_cubes.py
!scripts/out_cubes.json
scripts/test_queries.py
scripts/test_workarounds.py
scripts/test_resource_read.py
scripts/test_final.py

mockups/
.mockups/

# saved-view runtime store (VAULT_DIR)
views/

# Windows version-info resource — generated at build time by goversioninfo
# from go/versioninfo.json (see go/versioninfo.go, go/.goreleaser.yaml before.hooks)
*.syso

# cross-model critique scratch
.xcheck/

# Go build artifacts
go/bloxsmith
go/bloxsmith.exe
go/dist/
# Installers staged into go/ for goreleaser release.extra_files (see release.yml)
go/install.sh
go/install.ps1
# Static version file written by goreleaser's before-hook (.goreleaser.yaml)
go/version.json
go/web/app.bundle.js

# root-level templates/ is a fetched third-party copy — never commit (our own set lives in go/templates/)
/templates/
